## Weekly check-ins

To keep an overview of the current status of active tasks, team leads will write a **weekly check-in every weekend, usually on Saturday.**
Here's an example for a check-in:

> Hey team, here's the weekly check-in
> 
> @MalicousEasterBunny123 - Was doing some research. [Iwatodai Streets environment model](https://github.com/orgs/p3d-project/projects/1/views/1?filterQuery=label%3A%22%F0%9F%A7%8A+3d%22&pane=issue&itemId=208482391&issue=p3d-project%7Cpersona-3-dual%7C303). Still WIP. How's progress/any plans on what you will do?
> 
> @HappyHamster - Was doing some research. [Makoto character model](https://github.com/orgs/p3d-project/projects/1/views/1?filterQuery=label%3A%22%F0%9F%A7%8A+3d%22&pane=issue&itemId=208482391&issue=p3d-project%7Cpersona-3-dual%7C303) & [Iwatodai Dorm (lounge) environment model](https://github.com/orgs/p3d-project/projects/1/views/1?filterQuery=label%3A%22%F0%9F%A7%8A+3d%22&pane=issue&itemId=208482787&issue=p3d-project%7Cpersona-3-dual%7C304). Still WIP. How's progress/any plans on what you will do?
> 
> ...
> 
> All 3D issues are [here](https://github.com/orgs/p3d-project/projects/1/views/1?filterQuery=label%3A%22%F0%9F%A7%8A+3d%22)
> 
> If you're working on something but I've missed it, leave a message below.

This is to ensure no one gets stuck on a task, that the GitHub project board stays up to date, checking the current availability of individual team members and clarifying uncertainties on current tasks.

